## 1. Executive Summary

AlphaChart v3.4 is a self-improving, multi-timeframe, ensemble-based algorithmic paper trading system designed to achieve a **minimum 60% prediction success rate** on paper trades, with an aspirational target of **80–90%+**. The system trains and orchestrates multiple prediction engines — including FinRL-X reinforcement learning agents, a multi-timeframe technical analysis stack, and a LLM-based quality evaluator operating as a senior quant analyst — within a rigorous backtesting and risk-management framework.

Version 3.4 introduces six major advances over v3.3:

- **FinRL-X treated as expert signal input** to a hedge-fund-style multi-model ensemble
- **Full multi-timeframe processing** (3mo → intraday) with higher-timeframe anchoring
- **Continuous per-ticker and cross-ticker learning** via RLHF/RLMF and RAG memory
- **User-configurable growth target slider** (default: $10k → $100k / year) that dynamically modulates strategy aggressiveness within hard safety envelopes
- **BIOS-style GUI** with General (easy) and Advanced modes for all configuration
- **Automated portfolio and watchlist scanning** with live paper trading integration (Alpaca primary, IBKR fallback)

Phase 0 Backtest Audit (7-step protocol) remains the **hard blocking gate** — no model proceeds to live paper trading without passing it.

---

## 2. Key Architectural Decisions (v3.4)

- **FinRL-X Elevation:** FinRL-X outputs are no longer treated as primary signals. They are one expert input within a hedge-fund-style multi-model ensemble. The LLM layer synthesizes FinRL-X outputs alongside regime detectors, multi-timeframe trend filters, and ML factor models — exactly as a quantitative portfolio manager would review signals from a systematic sub-strategy.
- **Multi-Timeframe Stack:** A six-tier timeframe hierarchy (3mo, 1mo, 2wk, 1wk, daily, intraday) is implemented. Higher timeframes set directional bias and regime context; shorter timeframes provide entry/exit timing. Predictions are labeled by timeframe with explicit confidence decay at higher horizons.
- **LLM as Senior Quant, Not Voter:** The LLM layer is reframed as a quality evaluator and synthesis engine — it does not cast directional votes. It reads the full signal dossier (multi-timeframe summary, FinRL-X outputs, regime state, risk metrics) and returns a structured quality score, a risk flag, and a synthesis narrative. This eliminates the directional-voting failure mode from v3.3.
- **Continuous RLMF + RAG Learning:** The system records every trade outcome, labels it, and feeds it back into both the FinRL-X agents (reward shaping) and a persistent RAG vector store. Per-ticker and cross-ticker pattern libraries accumulate over time and are retrievable at inference.
- **Growth Target Slider:** A single master aggressiveness parameter, set via GUI slider, gates conviction thresholds, position sizing curves, and minimum quality scores — all bounded by immutable hard safety limits.
- **BIOS-Style GUI:** Two-tier UI: General Mode (clean, slider-based dashboard) and Advanced Mode (full parameter control over all subsystems). Streamlit implementation with tabs, expanders, and real-time status panels.
- **Portfolio Auto-Scan:** Alpaca API integration for live portfolio reads. All held tickers and watchlist tickers are automatically queued for signal generation on each run cycle.
- **Regime-Conditional Ensemble:** The ensemble weighting matrix is conditioned on detected market regime (TRENDING_UP, TRENDING_DOWN, RANGING, VOLATILE). Each regime has a separate calibrated weight vector. TREND_DOWN models are subject to additional scrutiny per v3.3 remediation rules.
- **Scoped State-Lock & Deterministic Safety Layer:** All inference paths pass through a deterministic rule-based safety filter before any order is staged. State-lock prevents conflicting signals from being acted upon simultaneously.
- **RSI Ablation Protocol Retained:** RSI-only signals are blocked. RSI is only used in multi-factor confirmation contexts.

