## 3. User Configuration System — BIOS-Style

### 3.1 Design Philosophy

The GUI configuration system is modeled on computer BIOS architecture: a **General Mode** (analogous to BIOS "Easy Mode") and an **Advanced Mode** (analogous to BIOS full configuration). Users enter General Mode by default. Advanced Mode is unlocked via a clearly labeled toggle/tab.

---

### 3.2 General Mode — Controls

**Growth Target Slider (Master Control)**

```
Label:  "Annual Growth Target"
Range:  $10,000 → $1,000,000  (log-scale)
Default: $100,000  (i.e., $10k → $100k = 10x / year)
Display: Shows implied monthly return %, required win-rate,
         and current aggressiveness tier (Conservative / Moderate / Aggressive / Max)
```

The slider maps to an **Aggressiveness Index (AI)** on a 0.0–1.0 scale:

| Slider Target (from $10k) | AI Value | Tier |
|---|---|---|
| $20k–$30k (2x–3x) | 0.0–0.25 | Conservative |
| $40k–$60k (4x–6x) | 0.25–0.55 | Moderate |
| $70k–$100k (7x–10x) | 0.55–0.80 | Aggressive |
| $100k–$1M (10x–100x) | 0.80–1.0 | Max (warnings shown) |

**Other General Mode Controls:**

| Control | Description | Default |
|---|---|---|
| Max Drawdown Tolerance | Portfolio-level stop | 15% |
| Max Single-Trade Risk | % of portfolio per trade | 3% |
| Auto-Trade vs. Approve | Auto-execute or require click-approval | Approve |
| Scan Interval | How often portfolio/watchlist is scanned | 15 min |
| Watchlist Tickers | Free-text + CSV import | — |
| Paper Broker | Alpaca / IBKR selector | Alpaca |

