### 5.2 Signal Generation Data Flow

```
INPUT: ticker, config (AI-modulated)
  │
  ├─► [1] DataFetcher
  │       → fetch OHLCV: 3mo, 1mo, 2wk, 1wk, daily, 60m, 15m
  │       → fetch fundamentals, news sentiment (optional)
  │       → cache with TTL per timeframe
  │
  ├─► [2] MultiTimeframeAnalyzer
  │       → compute per-timeframe: trend direction, momentum, structure
  │       → produce: TimeframeContext object (anchor bias + execution context)
  │
  ├─► [3] RegimeDetector
  │       → classify: TRENDING_UP / TRENDING_DOWN / RANGING / VOLATILE
  │       → select regime-conditional ensemble weight vector
  │
  ├─► [4] FinRL-X Engine
  │       → run trained PPO/SAC agents on current state vector
  │       → output: action probabilities, Q-values, agent confidence
  │       → tag as "expert signal" — not final decision
  │
  ├─► [5] MLFactorModel
  │       → compute: momentum, mean-reversion, vol-adjusted factors
  │       → output: factor score vector
  │
  ├─► [6] EnsembleAggregator
  │       → apply regime-conditional weights to all signals
  │       → compute: raw_conviction_score [0,1]
  │
  ├─► [7] DeterministicSafetyFilter
  │       → apply hard rules (gap filter, earnings blackout, etc.)
  │       → block or pass signal
  │
  ├─► [8] LLMQualityGate
  │       → send full signal dossier to LLM
  │       → receive: quality_score, risk_flags, narrative
  │       → if quality_score < min_quality_score: REJECT
  │
  ├─► [9] PositionSizer
  │       → compute: position_size, stop_loss, profit_target
  │       → apply AI-modulated sizing curve
  │
  └─► OUTPUT: TradingSignal object → OrderQueue / GUI
```

