## 12. Backtest Hygiene Rules & Non-Negotiable Constraints

### 12.1 Backtest Hygiene Rules

These rules apply at all times. Violation of any rule invalidates the backtest and restarts Phase 0.

```
RULE 1 — NO LOOKAHEAD BIAS
  All features must be computed using only data available at signal time T.
  No use of T+1 open, T+1 high, or any future price in feature construction.
  Validated by: data_leakage_check() in Phase 0 Step 1.

RULE 2 — POINT-IN-TIME DATA ONLY
  Fundamental data (earnings, splits, dividends) must be sourced from
  point-in-time databases. No revised data that wouldn't have been
  available at T.

RULE 3 — WALK-FORWARD MANDATORY
  Simple in-sample/out-of-sample splits are insufficient.
  Minimum 3 rolling walk-forward windows required.
  No parameter fitting on test windows.

RULE 4 — REGIME COVERAGE REQUIRED
  Training data must include all 4 regime types.
  Failing to cover TRENDING_DOWN in training produces invalidated SHORT-side models.

RULE 5 — TRANSACTION COST REALISM
  All backtest PnL calculations must include:
    - Commission: $0.005/share (Alpaca default)
    - Slippage model: 0.1% for liquid stocks, 0.3% for low-liquidity
    - Market impact: position_value / avg_daily_volume * 0.1

RULE 6 — NO BACKTEST OVERFITTING
  Any strategy with > 5 tuned parameters requires additional
  out-of-sample confirmation window beyond the standard 3.
  RSI-only strategies are unconditionally blocked.

RULE 7 — SURVIVORSHIP BIAS CONTROL
  Universe of tickers at time T must not include companies that
  were added to indices after T (forward-surviving bias).
  Use delisted ticker databases for historical tests.
```

---

### 12.2 Non-Negotiable Constraints

```
NC-1  Hard stop 5% max risk per trade — no override
NC-2  Hard stop 20% portfolio drawdown = full system halt, no new trades
NC-3  No entries within 2 calendar days of earnings announcement
NC-4  No trades in stocks with < 500,000 average daily volume
NC-5  RSI as sole signal is permanently blocked
NC-6  FinRL-X output alone is not sufficient for trade entry — ensemble required
NC-7  Phase 0 must pass before paper trading — no exceptions
NC-8  All orders are limit orders (no naked market orders) unless explicitly overridden
NC-9  LLM layer cannot override ensemble direction — quality gate only
NC-10 State-lock enforced: no duplicate concurrent orders on same ticker
NC-11 TRENDING_DOWN regime receives additional scrutiny on LONG signals
NC-12 All hard limits are code constants — not config values, not DB values
NC-13 Emergency stop button must be functional and halt all pending orders
NC-14 Minimum 60% out-of-sample win rate required before live paper trading
NC-15 Cross-ticker RAG learning must include recency weighting (decay half-life ≤ 90 days)
```

---

### 12.3 TREND_DOWN Remediation Protocol

When the regime detector identifies TRENDING_DOWN:

```python
TREND_DOWN_RULES = {
    "long_signal_conviction_penalty":  0.30,  # multiply conviction by 0.70
    "long_signal_quality_floor_raise": 0.10,  # raise min quality by 10pp
    "short_signal_conviction_boost":   0.10,  # multiply conviction by 1.10
    "require_multi_tf_long_alignment": True,  # all TFs must agree for LONG
    "max_long_position_size_pct":      0.02,  # cap LONG positions at 2%
    "finrl_x_agent_override": "ppo_TRENDING_DOWN"  # force regime-matched agent
}
```

---

## 13. Success Criteria

### 13.1 Primary Success Metrics

| Metric | Minimum | Target |
|---|---|---|
| Out-of-Sample Win Rate | 60% | 80–90% |
| Sharpe Ratio (paper trading) | 1.0 | ≥ 2.0 |
| Max Drawdown | < 20% | < 10% |
| Profit Factor | ≥ 1.3 | ≥ 2.0 |
| Annual Return (paper) | ≥ 50% | 900%+ (10x/year) |
| Phase 0 Audit Pass Rate | 100% | 100% (non-negotiable) |

---

### 13.2 System Quality Metrics

| Metric | Target |
|---|---|
| Signal generation latency (per ticker) | < 5 seconds |
| LLM quality gate latency | < 3 seconds |
| RAG retrieval latency | < 200ms |
| GUI scan cycle display refresh | < 10 seconds |
| Order submission latency | < 2 seconds |
| RLMF feedback incorporation lag | ≤ next retrain cycle |

---

### 13.3 Learning Improvement Criteria

The system is considered to be actively learning and improving if:

- Per-ticker win rate improves by ≥ 5% over first 100 trades on any ticker
- Cross-ticker RAG retrieval improves win rate on new tickers relative to baseline by ≥ 3%
- FinRL-X retrain events result in ≥ 5% win rate improvement in the triggered regime within 20 subsequent trades
- LLM quality score correlation with realized PnL: Pearson r ≥ 0.35

---

### 13.4 Definition of a Successful Prediction

A prediction is counted as **successful** if:

```python
def is_successful_prediction(signal: TradingSignal,
                              outcome: dict) -> bool:
    """
    Success = trade reached profit target before stop loss,
    OR trade was exited at time-based stop with positive PnL.
    """
    return outcome["won"] == True
    # where won = True iff:
    #   exit_reason in ["PROFIT_TARGET", "TIME_EXIT_POSITIVE"]
    #   AND pnl_pct > 0 after costs
```

